## 10. Linux Kernel & Intranet Network Tuning (`sysctl`)

Standard corporate Linux images have conservative TCP buffers and UDP queues that will bottleneck both **WireGuard/QUIC (P2P)** and **NCCL over TCP** on 10Gbps intranet links. Apply `/etc/sysctl.d/99-ml-intranet.conf` on all nodes:

```ini
# 1. Expand UDP/TCP socket buffers to 128MB (critical for Iroh QUIC & WireGuard throughput)
net.core.rmem_max = 134217728
net.core.wmem_max = 134217728
net.core.rmem_default = 16777216
net.core.wmem_default = 16777216
net.ipv4.tcp_rmem = 4096 87380 134217728
net.ipv4.tcp_wmem = 4096 65536 134217728

# 2. Switch TCP congestion control to BBR (handles cross-VLAN switch bufferbloat cleanly)
net.core.default_qdisc = fq
net.ipv4.tcp_congestion_control = bbr

# 3. Increase NIC packet backlog for bursty all_reduce / P2P swarm traffic
net.core.netdev_max_backlog = 250000

# 4. Allow high memory-map counts for Lance / Arrow / PyTorch shared memory
vm.max_map_count = 1048576
```

