## 11. Failure Modes & Recovery Matrix

| Failure Scenario | System Behavior & Automatic Mitigation |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Worker Node Reboots / Preempted** | KubeRay detects lost heartbeat; spins up replacement pod (or rescales world size via `torchrun` Elastic). New pod pulls latest `Checkpoint_CID` from surviving intranet peers via P2P. |
| **Corrupted Disk / Bit-Rot on NVMe** | Iroh/IPFS verifies BLAKE3/SHA-256 Merkle trees during transfer. Corrupted blocks fail cryptographic verification before atomic rename to `/var/cache/ml-shards/<cid>`. |
| **PostgreSQL Control DB Blip** | Active training **continues uninterrupted** for the remainder of the epoch because workers query Postgres only once at epoch start to fetch their shard manifest list. |
| **Slow / Congested Office Subnet** | If running **DiLoCo**, nodes sync outer gradients only every $H=200$ steps, absorbing transient intranet latency spikes with <2% throughput loss. |
| **Node NVMe Fills Up** | `cache-gc-agent` monitors disk usage every 30s; when >85%, deletes oldest `mtime` unpinned `.lance` files and removes corresponding rows from `node_cache_inventory`. |